BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Threads That Connect Us
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T160000
UID:ebd76bdfb70deb09e1f9484e6bcbe433@petalumaartscenter.org
DESCRIPTION:“Gaining From My Parents’ Loss” by Jorge de la Cal The T
 hreads That Connect Us Exhibition Dates: May 7 - June 6\, 2026 Opening Rec
 eption: Thursday\, May 7\, 5:30-7:30pm The Threads That Connect Us\, an ex
 hibition from the Origin Stories Project that weaves together storytelling
  and visual art to explore identity\, connection\, and the shared human ex
 perience. Each of the 70 works begins with a personal story—an identity-
 shaping moment of legacy\, arrival\, adversity\, or revelation. These narr
 atives are then transformed into Stories + Art Boxes using plexiglass encl
 osures where voice and visual expression are experienced together. At its 
 core\, the project is grounded in a simple belief: when people share their
  stories and truly listen to one another\, connection grows. This exhibiti
 on brings together works from the permanent collection alongside a Gen Z s
 howcase featuring Northern California students. The Gen Z component offers
  an intergenerational perspective on resilience\, self-discovery\, and bel
 onging. #block-635d83d9438605f6fa53 { --stroke-style: none\;--stroke-thick
 ness: 6px\; --tweak-text-block-background-color: initial\; } #block-635d83
